      "key": "ShortcutManager",
      "kind": "singleton",
      "doc": {
        "summary": "ShortcutManager is a singleton class that manages global keyboard shortcuts.",
        "details": "The ShortcutManager provides centralized access to system-wide keyboard shortcut registration and handling. It follows the singleton pattern to ensure there's only one instance managing all shortcuts throughout the application lifetime.\n\nKey features:\n- Singleton pattern ensures centralized shortcut management\n- Event-driven architecture for shortcut activation notifications\n- Cross-platform shortcut registration and monitoring\n- Thread-safe access to the singleton instance\n- Automatic cleanup of resources on destruction\n- Support for both global and application-local shortcuts",
        "notes": [
          {
            "kind": "note",
            "text": "This class is thread-safe for singleton access and shortcut operations."
          },
          {
            "kind": "note",
            "text": "Shortcut instances should be created and managed through this manager."
          }
        ]
      },
