          "key": "ShortcutManager::Register",
          "kind": "method",
          "doc": {
            "summary": "Register a new global keyboard shortcut.",
            "details": "Creates and registers a new keyboard shortcut that can be triggered system-wide, regardless of which application has focus. The shortcut will trigger the provided callback when activated.\n\n**Example**\n\n```cpp\nauto shortcut = manager.Register(\"Ctrl+Shift+Q\", []() {\n    std::cout << \"Quick action triggered!\" << std::endl;\n});\n\nif (!shortcut) {\n    std::cerr << \"Failed to register shortcut\" << std::endl;\n}\n```",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "accelerator",
                "text": "The keyboard shortcut string (e.g., \"Ctrl+Shift+A\", \"Cmd+Space\")"
              },
              {
                "name": "callback",
                "text": "Function to call when the shortcut is activated"
              }
            ],
            "returns": "Shared pointer to the created Shortcut instance, nullptr if registration failed",
            "notes": [
              {
                "kind": "thread_safety",
                "text": "This method is thread-safe"
              },
              {
                "kind": "note",
                "text": "Accelerator format follows Electron-style conventions:\n- Modifiers: Ctrl, Alt, Shift, Cmd (macOS), Super (Linux), Meta\n- Keys: A-Z, 0-9, F1-F12, Space, Tab, Enter, Escape, etc.\n- Examples: \"Ctrl+C\", \"Cmd+Shift+4\", \"Alt+F4\", \"Ctrl+Alt+Delete\""
              }
            ]
          },
