        {
          "key": "ShortcutManager::SetEnabled",
          "kind": "method",
          "doc": {
            "summary": "Enable or disable shortcut processing.",
            "details": "Allows temporarily disabling all shortcut processing without unregistering shortcuts. When disabled, shortcuts will remain registered but won't trigger their callbacks. This is useful for modal dialogs or when the application needs to temporarily suppress shortcut handling.\n\n**Example**\n\n```cpp\n// Disable shortcuts during modal dialog\nmanager.SetEnabled(false);\nShowModalDialog();\nmanager.SetEnabled(true);  // Re-enable after dialog closes\n```",
